  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Trestle Light",
    "description": "A slim green-and-white lighthouse on a rock out in the water, reached only along a timber trestle bridge from the shore. Its lantern burns green after dark in World View, the starboard light at a harbour mouth, and its window glows with lamplight. 32 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Rock** — two dark Block 2x2s side by side make a rock, 4 by 2, standing out of the water, with Rocks round its foot.\n2. **Shore** — two Wide Stairs (the upper one on a Brick 1x2, turned 90°, press **R**) climb onto a stone Block 2x2, where the bridge starts.\n3. **Trestle Bridge** — two Diagonal Braces, turned 90° and 270°, cross in an X out in the water to make the trestle. Two wooden Plate 2x4s, turned 90°, run from the shore over the trestle to the rock, with four Fences along each side for railings.\n4. **Tower** — a Round Plate 2x2 on the far half of the rock, so the bridge lands on open stone, then two Pillars, white and green. The Door, turned 90°, faces the bridge; a Small Window in the green band glows with lamplight at night.\n5. **Lantern** — a Round Plate 2x2, a green Lantern that shines green after dark, another Round Plate 2x2 and a green Cone Roof.\n\nStand it with the first step on the shore and the rest out over the water: the bridge is the only way across.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Rock: 2 Block 2x2, 5 Rock\n- Shore: 2 Wide Stair, 1 Brick 1x2, 1 Block 2x2\n- Trestle Bridge: 2 Diagonal Brace 2x2, 2 Plate 2x4, 8 Fence\n- Tower: 1 Round Plate 2x2, 2 Pillar, 1 Door, 1 Small Window\n- Lantern: 2 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Cone Roof\n\n32 bricks in all.\n",
